    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50163" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vānĭlŏquus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-lŏcus</span></b> ),
			a, um, adj.
		vanus-loquor, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>talking emplily</i> or <i>idly</i>,
				<i>gabbling</i>, <i>prating</i>, i.
			e., </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Lying</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quia vanilocu's, vapulabis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Am. 1, 1, 223</span></i>
			.— <i><span class="en">Ambros. Ep. 63,
			7</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Boastful</i>, <i>bragging</i>, <i>vaunting</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 35,
				48, 2</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ore,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					14, 280</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">genus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 8,
					17</span></i>
			.</div>
